      "finding": "A typographical error in the source, not an extraction error and not a physics error. T0/T = 1 + (gamma-1)/2 M^2 is exactly linear in M^2, so at M = 16 and gamma = 1.4 it is exactly 52.2 -- no rounding is involved at all. All 216 other printed rows satisfy that identity at printed precision; this one row is out by 18 half-units, and its neighbours at M = 15 (46.00) and M = 17 (58.80) are both exact. The digits appear transposed: 5220 printed as 5229.",
